=== input collection ===
NIN           @ the number to check
CPY A RX

=== handle n = 0 or 1 edge cases ===
JLS RX [2] na

=== prepare memory ===
CPY [2] RY    @ the current integer being divided

=== main loop ===
) loop
@ if RY^2 > RX, and the loop is still going (meaning
@ it passed), the number is prime
MUL RY RY
JGR A RX prime

@ if RX % RY == 0, the number is not prime
DIV RX RY
MUL A RY
SUB RX A
JEQ A [0] composite

@ increment RY and loop
INC RY
JMP loop

=== primality check indeterminate ===
) na
OUT [?] @ N (78)
OUT [l] @ / (47)
OUT [$] @ A (65)
HLT

=== primality check passed (prime) ===
) prime
OUT [13] @ T (84)
HLT

=== primality check failed (not prime) ===
) composite
OUT [+]  @ F (70)
HLT
